Oh wow, that makes total sense! I bet you're right about the API response structure being different than I expected. Let me try adding some debugging prints to see what's actually in there.

I just ran it with the print statements you suggested, and you're absolutely right - the structure is completely different. It looks like the API is returning something like:

```json
{
  "data": {
    "entries": [
      {"title": "Item 1", "id": 123},
      {"title": "Item 2", "id": 124}
    ]
  },
  "status": "success"
}
```

So I need to access `data['entries'][0]['title']` instead. That's embarrassing - I was working off old documentation apparently!

Quick follow-up though - I'm also getting some intermittent timeout errors when calling this API. Sometimes it works fine, other times it just hangs for like 30 seconds before failing. Any ideas on how to make this more robust? I was thinking of adding a timeout parameter to the requests.get() call, but I'm not sure what's a reasonable value.

